// File:    std/compiler_safety_test.skink
// Purpose: Runtime safety regression tests for emitted code:
//            comp_error.md #149 — string element access s[i] / s[i] = c
//              is now bounds-checked (reads previously walked past the
//              allocation — info leak; writes corrupted the heap).
//            comp_error.md #150 — integer division/remainder by zero,
//              INT_MIN / -1, INT_MIN % -1, and out-of-range shift
//              counts panic instead of emitting LLVM undefined behavior.
//          Runs standalone (module main); panics are caught with
//          defer/recover wrappers.
